 Factor-less identities keep the terminal CHALLENGE; no `THREAT_MODEL.md` row moved (`tests/integration/test_step_up.py`, `tests/adversarial/test_step_up_adversarial.py`). First-run reset (38) — `scripts/reset_dev_state.py` is the one canonical dev reset (CLI confirms unless `--yes`; clears the Redis keys, five tables incl. `approvals`, and — CLI/demo only — the revision snapshots that would still trip item 19's append-only check), delegated to by the demo, benchmarks, and the `clean_audit` fixture (test callers pass `clear_snapshots=False`); a boot-time `ActivationError` is logged and re-raised by `main._record_startup_activation` with the exact reset commands, check unweakened (`tests/integration/test_first_run_reset.py`).

**Rule for this phase: never make a `THREAT_MODEL.md` row more optimistic than the code.** A row moves only when the item that earns it is actually built and its `verify:` check passes — that inversion (claims outrunning implementation) is the exact failure Phase 5 exists to correct, and re-introducing it is worse than the original bug. Build order, and it was deliberate: 31–33 landed first and fast (defects, not features), then 34 (the centrepiece), 35 (the invasive refactor — the server registry), 36 (description integrity), 37 (step-up auth — the TOTP challenge/redeem flow), and 38 (first-run state reset) closed it out. **Phase 5 is complete** — the only open roadmap items are Phase 4's deliberately deferred Terraform (24) and the demo screen recording (operator step).

